import site/games/progress/goals.dl

set coding to new website coding progress for "farm"
require condition ((record website coding goal "eggs" amount 0 in coding) = false) reporting "Zero collected eggs changed progress."
require condition (record website coding goal "eggs" amount 4 in coding) reporting "Collected eggs were not counted."
require condition (record website coding goal "eggs" amount 2 in coding) reporting "Another collection was treated as a duplicate."
require condition ((record website coding goal "eggs" amount (-1) in coding) = false) reporting "Negative progress changed a goal."
require condition (((the website coding count of "eggs" in coding) = 6) and ((the JSON member named "seen" in (the JSON member named "eggs" in coding))'s length = 0)) reporting "Unkeyed goals acquired deduplication keys."
require condition (record website coding goal "planting" using key "🌽,north" in coding) reporting "A distinct Unicode bed was not counted."
require condition ((record website coding goal "planting" using key "🌽,north" in coding) = false) reporting "A planted bed was counted twice."
require condition ((the website coding count of "planting" in coding) = 1) reporting "Unique bed counts changed."
require condition (record website coding goal "watering" amount (4294967296 as a 64 bit integer) in coding) reporting "A portable 64-bit goal quantity was lost."
require condition ((the website coding count of "watering" in coding) = (4294967296 as a 64 bit integer)) reporting "Goal quantities were truncated on this target."
free coding
set river to new website coding progress for "river"
require condition (record website coding goal "passenger" using key "sheep" in river) reporting "The River goal API stopped recording passengers."
require condition ((record website coding goal "passenger" using key "sheep" in river) = false) reporting "The River goal API stopped deduplicating passengers."
free river
print line "Coding goals count collected quantities and distinct Unicode targets without changing River progress."
